# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Mutation testing output — reports/ and Stryker working dirs are
# regenerated by `npm run test:mutation`, never committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
reports/
.stryker-tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Kubic's own local state. The checkout's `.kubic/` directory holds local
# project config, role documents and run state, and none of it is committed,
# so a contributor's config can never leak into a commit. The documented
# example of a project config is packages/host/src/config/example.toml.
#
# The runtime subpaths are listed as well: `kubic doctor` checks the ignore
# file for the same rules `kubic run` writes into a user repo's exclude file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.kubic/
.kubic/sessions/
.kubic/journal/
.kubic/artifacts/
.kubic/audit/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private agent instructions: the development process of the AI agents that
# build Kubic. Local only, deliberately not part of the released codebase
# (public files must not reference or depend on it).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
AGENTS.md
/CLAUDE.md
